{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-71430",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To find the number of pages Suzie can read in $1$ hour, we compute the unit rate of pages per hour. We do this by dividing the number of pages Suzie reads, $22,$ by the number of hours, $\\frac{2}{3},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n22÷\\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}22÷\\frac{2}{3} & =22\\times \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{22}{1}\\times \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{22\\times 3}{1\\times 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{66}{2} \\\\  & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Suzie can read $33$ pages in $1$ hour.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
